The implementation uses a simple counter to track the balance of open and close brackets:
1. For every opening bracket '(', it increments the balance.
2. For every closing bracket ')', it decrements the balance.
3. If at any point the balance goes negative, we have an unmatched closing bracket, so we immediately return false.
4. After processing all characters, if the balance is zero, the brackets are properly matched.

This approach works in O(n) time complexity where n is the length of the input string, which is efficient for this type of problem.

