The helper function `isApproximatelyEqual` compares two doubles for approximate equality by checking if their absolute difference is smaller than a specified tolerance level, defaulting to $10^{-6}$. This helps mitigate issues related to floating-point precision while still maintaining accuracy for typical use cases.

